{
  "version": "1.0",
  "name": "Tutorial 4: The Echo Chamber",
  "description": "Watch how RNN remembers previous inputs!\n\nThis network has MEMORY. When you input 1.0, then switch to 0.0,\nthe output doesn't immediately drop - it slowly decays like an echo.\n\nHOW IT WORKS:\n- The RNN has a hidden state that persists between steps\n- Each step, the hidden state mixes old memory with new input\n- Output gradually fades as old information decays\n\nTRY THIS:\n1. Set input to 1.0, run several steps - watch output rise\n2. Set input to 0.0, run more steps - watch the 'echo' fade\n3. Reset states and see the echo disappear instantly\n\nThis is WHY recurrent networks are used for sequences -\nthey remember what came before.",
  "metadata": {
    "created": "2025-12-19T20:45:00.000000",
    "modified": "2025-12-19T20:45:00.000000",
