      "name": "Welcome",
      "position": [
        50,
        50
      ],
      "params": {
        "text": "# Echo Chamber - Memory in Networks\n\nThis tutorial shows how **recurrence** lets networks remember.\n\n## To Do and Notice\n\n1. **Feed a signal**: Watch how it persists even after input stops\n2. **The feedback loop**: Output feeds back to input\n3. **Decay**: Notice how memory fades over time without reinforcement\n\n## Why This Matters\n\nRecurrence is the foundation of:\n- Language models (remembering context)\n- Time series prediction\n- Music generation\n\n**Challenge**: Can you make the memory last longer by adjusting weights?",
        "width": 450,
        "show_on_start": true
      },
      "inputs": {},
      "outputs": {},
      "weights": {},
      "collapsed": false,
      "color": "#5c4a3d",
      "tags": [],
      "description": "Tutorial introduction"
    }
